      "title": "complexity-mass — Σ cyclomatic complexity over those functions",
      "description": "Read beside functions, which is the whole reason both are carried. Mass and functions rising by the same amount is dilution — thirty trivial functions appended beside a bad one — while mass flat with functions up is a split. Neither game moves a ratio, which is why this page shows counts and derives no share. ⚠️ Where one plotted point covers several runs it shows the HIGHEST among them, because for this count the unflattering direction is up. No target line and no threshold: mass grows with the codebase legitimately.",
