      "id": 10,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "complexity-mass-over-10 — Σ complexity in functions above McCabe's cut",
      "description": "Σ complexity over the functions whose own complexity exceeds 10. ⚠️ The cut is McCabe's 1976 upper bound for a module. It is a sourced constant inside this measure's definition and NOT a threshold — nothing goes red when a function crosses it, and no line is drawn for it here. ⚠️ Where one plotted point covers several runs it shows the HIGHEST among them, because for this count the unflattering direction is up. Read against mass: this rising while mass holds means the same branches concentrated into fewer, larger functions.",
