      "title": "complexity-max — the largest single function",
      "description": "The highest complexity of any one function in the scope. ⚠️ A fall here while mass held is a split, not a simplification: the branches moved into new functions rather than going away. The prototype measured exactly that — a mechanical three-way split of this repo's worst function dropped max by 10 while mass ROSE by 5. That is the reading this panel exists for, and it is why max is never read alone. ⚠️ Where one plotted point covers several runs it shows the HIGHEST among them. No target line: read against the scope's own history.",
