    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "The instrument: what the suite and a mutation run cost",
      "description": "Mutation cost scales with suite runtime, and `mutation-run-runtime` is the series that says when running this on every merge becomes affordable. Neither is a verdict on the code. ⚠️ Where one plotted point covers several runs it is the SLOWEST of them — the non-flattering direction for a cost, which is why this panel reduces the opposite way to panel 2. `gate-suite-runtime` is written on every push to main, so this one bins more often than the nightly does.",
